{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The son of Hagar the Egyptian.</b> She supposed that he was stirred to this mockery because he had heard such things from his mother, as the Sages said (Sukkah 56b): שׁוּתָא דִּינוּקָא בְּשׁוּקָא אוֹ דְּאָבוּהִי אוֹ דְּאִימֵּיהּ — 'a child's prattle in the marketplace is either from his father or from his mother.'" "<b>Mocking.</b> Mocking the feast that was held in Abraham's household, saying that she had conceived from Abimelech. And the reason this did not happen at the time of Isaac's birth is that Ishmael heard such things only afterward from the scoffers of that generation; and even if he had been mocking at the time of the birth — Sarah would not have noticed, for she was then preoccupied."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:58.931246538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}